The semileptonic decays of doubly charmed baryons $D_{cc} 	o \Lambda_c \ell  ar{
u}$ and $D_{cc} 	o  ar{D} \ell  ar{\mathrm{c}}$ are investigated using the bag model. The form factors for these decays are calculated and their numerical values are presented. The estimated branching ratios for $D_{cc} 	o \Lambda_c \mu  ar{
u}$ and $D_{cc} 	o \Lambda_c 	au  ar{
u}$ are found to be $1.1 	imes 10^{-4}$ and $2.1 	imes 10^{-5}$, respectively. The estimated branching ratios for $D_{cc} 	o  ar{D} \mu  ar{\mathrm{c}}$ and $D_{cc} 	o  ar{D} 	au  ar{\mathrm{c}}$ are found to be $2.1 	imes 10^{-4}$ and $1.1 	imes 10^{-4}$, respectively. The results indicate that the doubly charmed baryon $D_{cc}$ is a suitable candidate for studying the charged lepton flavor universality violation.
